    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "What these insights can and cannot show",
      "type": "text",
      "description": "",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 4
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "noValue": "N/A",
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "blue",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Overflows** describe scenario activity, not unique attackers. Tests and internal events are included in native counters. The email report separates them using LAPI event data and identifies service + host, IP, country and ASN. Those dimensions cannot be invented from aggregate metrics. Current retained alerts and active decision records are separate inventories."
      }
    },
